A key that renders into a path rather than a name is refused: the error names the config
path and the rendered name, and the empty receipt shows nothing was written — the
destination is never even created.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  e2e_demo:
    tree:
      "{{ slug }}.md": "body\n"
-- cmd --
booping scaffold core.e2e_demo.tree out --set slug=../escape
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: core.e2e_demo.tree.{{ slug }}.md: unsafe filename key '../escape.md'
